{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The latest centering experiment produced a nonzero attention correction, but its AUC stayed below the strongest pooling control. Its added head also reads the full pooled feature set, so it can learn from redundant evidence.\n\nI’ll prepare a tied-head contrast that subtracts the head’s pooled-only output. It becomes zero when the attention correction is zero. A matched history-query variant will test the value of using the target as the query; two variants leave roughly 1,800 seconds for host assessment.\n"}}
