centered_null 0.6303864702, but remains below pooled_reference 0.6307714975; target Logloss 0.1926526373 also exceeds null 0.1926389704. Candidate-supplied correction RMS 0.836 and checkpoint logit shift 0.0386 show implementation activity, not utility. Empirical priors previously gave target/context AUC 0.6303523996/0.6303489998, and radius_target 0.6306798923 remained below the stronger pooled control. Provisional mechanism: an unconstrained extra head over all inherited features may spend capacity relearning pooled evidence instead of learning the attention correction. Test parent + h(X,p+d)-h(X,p), using exactly the inherited head twice with tied weights. This removes the independent h(X,p) shortcut. If useful target-specific corrections exist, the target version may improve over the history-query replacement and pooled references. This is an untested explanation, not evidence that shortcut learning caused prior failures.',\n  'nearest_work':[\n   {'source_ref':'paper:din, arXiv:1706.06978v4 section 4.3 lines 250-277; content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2','verification':'read','difference':'Inherit ad-conditioned local scoring and weighted history aggregation. DIN explicitly abandons softmax; this study keeps the inherited balanced group softmax and signed weight centering. New local intervention is tied predictor subtraction, not DIN replication or a verified general novelty claim.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0022-centered_target; source-sha256:88af225ebceb99c867ea7ccbb9e4cdd6aa26bf4546af78e2da1bc714d0cb5dfa','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Preserve all source classes and _centered_read. Replace only additive h(X,p+d) by h(X,p+d)-h(X,p); reuse the same head with no allocation, new inputs, fitted scale or extra randomness.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0020-pooled_reference; source-sha256:c7afb27541d642ee27bce4d54755406b29a3605d140453a71e8c9087882a123b','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'This strongest observed utility control uses only a global pooled summary in its extra head. Preserve it as a historical performance/cost reference. Its trained result is not an independently retrained matched null for the new contrast.'},\n   {'source_ref':'paper:dmr; author README commit 2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9 lines 1-9; content-sha256:656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75','verification':'read','difference':'Respect category/brand/type fields without inventing item identities. Publisher paper unavailable; no detailed DMR mechanism or priority claim.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':['Host-owned data construction, scoring, resource ledger and frozen information boundary; no raw-data access or local training','Full g1-r0019-pooled_observed predictor and all identity/context/repeat/overlap/transition/gap heads','g3-r0022-centered_target balanced within-match-group signed correction d=sum((w-u)*value), with separate field reads','Same dormant-parent attention activated as scorer, embeddings, head allocation order, initialization and training recipe','Archived industry cards and latest usage/outcome record reviewed; no source architecture newly adopted'],\n  'proposed_difference':'Only the readout-to-logit map changes: with inherited bias-free W,V and ReLU, a=W[X,p], b=W_summary*d, return parent+V(ReLU(a+b)-ReLU(a)). In real arithmetic this is h(X,p+d)-h(X,p), with shared weights, identical allocated parameter count 17,270,691 in the frozen metadata, and exactly zero residual for d=0. Both query modes execute the same graph. Neither input nor logits are detached. This differs from input centering: the preceding study centered weights but still retained independent h(X,p) capacity. The new head retains conditional interactions with X; it does not remove all extra function capacity. General novelty remains unverified.',\n  'predictions':['Algebraic: null correction d=0 gives exactly zero residual for every X,p and parameter setting; empty histories also yield zero new residual. Explicit two-head and efficient preactivation implementations agree within float32 tolerance; inherited parent reproduction remains within 1e-5 on the fixed probe.','Empirical, uncertain: tied_target exceeds tied_context and both frozen source bests (pooled_observed AUC 0.6302753101, balanced_target 0.6202303849), and must also exceed the stronger pooled_reference AUC 0.6307714975 before suggesting useful complementarity. Report Logloss separately.','The tied contrast should have the same allocated and active head/scorer capacity in target/context variants, with training/inference cost close to centered variants; the narrow W_summary*d product adds compute but no parameters. All host cost measurements are decisive.','Predeclared descriptive slices use host bins/counts for history length, hour, action presence, match presence and training frequency. In particular history>64 has 3,026,583 validation rows/151,372 positives; empty has 8,272/310. Examine heterogeneity without selecting by slice maxima or claiming confirmatory significance.'],\n  'falsifiers':['Target fails to exceed strongest pooled_reference or the target-query replacement; a positive diagnostic or improvement over only the weaker source does not establish complementarity.','Logloss deterioration, excessive measured inference/training cost, or an advantage explained by a historical duplicate-evidence control prevents an unqualified performance claim.','Nonzero null residual, discrepancy from explicit tied-head oracle beyond normal float32 error, nonfinite empty/zero-length outputs, or order/padding errors invalidate the implementation before mechanism interpretation.','A single-seed ordering is not repeated support; if later paired seeds reverse it, retain an inconclusive outcome. No test feedback is available or authorized.'],\n  'alternative_explanations':['Across nominal pooled nulls AUC ranges from empirical_uniform 0.6300724490 to pooled_reference 0.6307714975 despite near-equal checkpoint algebra. Finite-precision computation, optimization trajectories, allocation-dependent RNG effects or winner selection remain unseparated; no single explanation is established.','Tied subtraction can reduce useful additive capacity or change optimization/regularization. Failure would reject this implementation, not all target conditioning.','Context replaces only the query with a history-field mean. Match partitions, static features and the full predictor still use the target, so this does not test total target independence.','Shared head cancellation eliminates a standalone pooled term but leaves additional nonlinear interactions. Historical duplicate/capacity controls are useful utility anchors, not fresh causal controls for this map. A winning target still needs a newly trained active duplicate-evidence replacement and paired repetitions.','Static publisher snapshots have undocumented as-of dates; this remains a benchmark assumption. Category/brand histories are coarser than item sequences; no transfer from external conversion studies is established.','First-512 candidate diagnostics establish local code properties only; no labels, population generalization or causal interpretation follows.'],\n  'contrasts':[\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0022-centered_target','intervention':'tied_target: replace only h(X,p+d) by h(X,p+d)-h(X,p), preserving target query and correction','control':'g3-r0022-centered_target is the historical additive-head single-change control; g3-r0020-pooled_reference and g1-r0019-pooled_observed remain mandatory utility comparators','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['No new paired seed or host checkpoint replay for the historical additive result','Tied subtraction changes gradients and available additive function capacity; these are the intervention, not proof of the shortcut hypothesis','Standalone full-source hashes and host measurements are required; no local Torch execution is available'],'decision_if_supported':'Treat as provisional evidence for useful tied-readout parameterization; do not assert shortcut mechanism or novelty. Freeze source/config and closest controls before any authorized final validation assessment.','decision_if_not_supported':'Keep pooled_reference as best supported utility model. Record a negative continuation of the centering branch; do not tune coefficient/temperature or consume assessment reserve.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0022-centered_context','intervention':'tied_target uses current category/brand field embeddings as the two scorer queries','control':'tied_context uses history-mean category/brand queries with exactly the same tied contrast and all allocations; active scorer replacement','held_fixed':held+['tied subtraction algebra, selected correction weighting and fully shared comparison implementation'],'remaining_confounds':['Group membership and full static features remain target-dependent','Independent optimization can diverge despite matched initialization and seed','No independently trained active duplicate-evidence version fits alongside conservative final reserve; historical raw_pooled_duplicate and pooled_reference are performance anchors only'],'decision_if_supported':'Support only incremental query choice under this contrast and seed, contingent on beating the strongest pooled reference. Next falsifiable question is whether that ordering survives an active pooled-keys replacement and paired seeds.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not claim target-query utility; conclude evidence remains insufficient and preserve all negative results.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'Label-free analytic null d=0 through the new tied head, plus same-checkpoint explicit head-difference oracle','control':'New residual must vanish identically, leaving inherited pooled_observed logits at the same weights; compare the archived trained source for utility only','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Analytic null is not a newly trained null and cannot explain historical null dispersion','Head can still create interactions with redundant X even when driven by nonzero d'],'decision_if_supported':'Establish the intended no-independent-shortcut code property only. Keep capacity attribution provisional.','decision_if_not_supported':'Implementation invalid: stop and retain failed cost, rather than interpreting predictive results.'}\n  ],\n  'cost_plan':{\n   'estimate_ref':'run://r-001 remaining_seconds=4147.271939277649; g3-r0022-centered_target wall=1060.29, context=1036.76, null=1045.05; g3-r0020-pooled_reference wall=1038.80; unit cap=1760.9324324010606 seconds. Estimate 1100-1150 seconds per new variant, with no extra embedding/scoring pass in forward.',\n   'all_variants_counted':True,\n   'attribution_reserve':'One new candidate plus one active history-query replacement, budget <=2300 seconds estimated total including diagnostics/validation. No calibration, learning-rate screens, synthetic training, hidden retries or installations. Local syntax/source/algebra preparation is charged. Do not add a third exploratory variant.',\n   'assessment_reserve':'Preserve at least one hard-cap unit (1760.94 seconds) plus approximately 86 seconds of estimate slack from the starting 4147.27 seconds. Only launch if current ledger permits both proposed units and reserve. Validation-only assessment, no test. Three paired seeds for candidate plus closest controls cannot fit the remaining budget: explicitly omit rather than claim repeated support. If a new result is promising but reserve permits only one repetition, report limited single-seed attribution and preserve sources/comparison suite before assessment.',\n   'stop_rule':'Host hard limits and ledger prevail. No local training. Stop research if measured first unit makes the second plus assessment reserve infeasible; do not automatically retry unknown or failed execution states. If no target improvement over strongest pooled_reference, retain it and spend only authorized final assessment resources. No budget increases, no withheld requests, no adaptive holdout reuse.'\n  }\n },\n 'parent_trial':'g3-r0022-centered_target',\n 'variants':[],\n 'knowledge_assessments':[]\n}\nfor name,mode,role in [('tied_target','target','candidate'),('tied_context','context','control')]:\n cfg={**config,'fusion_mode':mode}\n proposal['variants'].append({'name':name,'file':name+'.py','role':role,'config':cfg,'note':('Tied ReLU activation difference; target query.' if mode=='target' else 'Active history-mean query replacement; grouping and full predictor still target-dependent.')+' Same inherited parameters and optimizer; host instantiates Model(meta, config) and runs frozen training automatically. No local training or measured new performance. Syntax/source/algebra checks pending; Torch unavailable. Diagnostics are label-free and candidate-supplied.'})\nitems=[\n ('taac2026-academic-1-craft','considered','Card and inherited usage reviewed. No measured propagation instability or reliable-field evidence; no reliability gate or transport architecture adopted.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-2-unidac','rejected','Organizer summary only; frozen input has no separate older-history stream. No history expansion, domain paths or feedback gates.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer','rejected','No local token-allocation bottleneck established; no token expansion or generated interest tokens.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-1-queryformer','considered','No established query-construction bottleneck. Test simple active history-query replacement before adding generated probes or packed views; no source architecture adopted.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-2-unidot','considered','Inherited usage and card report metric disagreement, so report AUC and Logloss separately. No highway, bus, auxiliary task or optimizer imported.'),\n ('paper:din','used','Primary v4 section 4.3 lines 250-277 read. Inherit local relevance query and scorer; unlike DIN retain group softmax. New intervention is tied logit subtraction, not a source-specific reproduction.'),\n ('paper:dmr','unresolved','Read pinned author README lines 1-9, respecting absence of item identities. Publisher full text unavailable; no detailed mechanism attribution.')]\nfor kid,decision,reason in items:\n proposal['knowledge_assessments'].append({'knowledge_id':kid,'decision':decision,'rationale':reason,'transformed_mechanism':'Inherited target-aware scorer with tied nonlinear readout subtraction; no newly adopted industry mechanism.' if kid=='paper:din' else 'No new architecture adopted from this source.','variant_names':['tied_target','tied_context'] if kid=='paper:din' else [],'nearest_work_difference':'Same centered history correction and capacity as g3-r0022-centered_target; subtract a tied pooled-reference head to eliminate its standalone output. General novelty unverified.','falsifier':'Target fails against active history-query replacement or strongest pooled_reference, null does not cancel, or later matched duplication/repetition reproduces the gain.'})\nPath('/workspace/proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote prospective proposal.json with two variants, controls, source provenance, failed directions and reserve.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
